## Proposed Changes

### Component: Database Migrations & Security

#### [NEW] [012_security_triggers.sql](file:///d:/TechPlatform/skillarena/supabase/migrations/012_security_triggers.sql)
- Formally define the security triggers inside the migrations directory.
- Refactor trigger functions to check against `profiles.role` (allowing admins and instructors to update status/roles/scores) rather than checking against `auth.role() = 'authenticated'`:
  - `protect_profile_fields()`: Only allow `admin` users to modify `role`, `xp`, `level` or `streak_days` columns. If updated by a student, revert these fields to their original values.
  - `protect_submission_fields()`: Only allow `admin` or `instructor` (or the system runner for auto-approved MCQ types) to modify a submission's `status`, `score` or `feedback`.

#### [NEW] [013_performance_indexes.sql](file:///d:/TechPlatform/skillarena/supabase/migrations/013_performance_indexes.sql)
- Formally move performance indexes from `create_indexes.js` to a tracked migration file:
  - `idx_lessons_course_id` on `lessons(course_id)`
  - `idx_assignments_lesson_id` on `assignments(lesson_id)`
  - `idx_submissions_user_id` on `submissions(user_id)`
  - `idx_submissions_assignment_id` on `submissions(assignment_id)`
  - `idx_submissions_status` on `submissions(status)`
  - `idx_enrollments_user_id` on `enrollments(user_id)`
  - `idx_lesson_progress_user_id` on `lesson_progress(user_id)`
  - `idx_xp_log_user_id` on `xp_log(user_id)`

#### [MODIFY] [002_rls_policies.sql](file:///d:/TechPlatform/skillarena/supabase/migrations/002_rls_policies.sql)
- Restructure the update policy for `enrollments` table. Splitting the broad `FOR ALL` policy into separate `INSERT`, `SELECT`, and `UPDATE` policies.
- Ensure that students can only update `progress` or `completed_at` values, while `status` updates are only permitted for instructors and admins.

---

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- We will write a unit test script under `scratch/test_security_policies.js` using the standard database connection to simulate:
  - Profile modification attempt by a student user: verifying that sensitive fields (role, xp) are rejected/reverted by database triggers.
  - Enrollment update attempt: verifying that a student cannot change their own enrollment status to 'approved'.
